 "description": "bigville R20 (268000): TWO-TIER COUNCIL GOVERNANCE. cm_convene fires a meeting on the R3-time CADENCE (Mod(now_day,cadence)==0). cm_public_address reads the mayor's benevolent ADDRESS onto the meeting; cm_attendee_hears_address delivers that PUBLIC content to attendees. cm_member_vote is the PRIVATE deliberation on the council backing-graph: vote = captured ? (base+malice*self_serving_premium) : public_demand (a captured council ignores the town; a responsive one tracks it). cm_private_decision sets held_decision = mean vote over has_member (the collective decision_value). cm_attendee_hears_decision delivers the decision to the town ONLY when the private tier is ablated (private_on==0) -- else the room is occluded (R19 observe-vs-hear). cm_institutional_gap = |address - decision| is the 234 stated!=held atom at institutional scale (ablate malice -> gap closes). Composes existing Terms (IfThenElse/Eq/And/Abs/Plus/Minus/Times/IDiv/Mod/Sum/Count/Neighbours/Attr/Var/Lit) -- zero new Rust. self_load_only. AUDIT 6.8 (block 348000): cm_convene's Mod(now_day,cadence) scheduling is a LEGACY FORCED CLOCK, superseded for scheduling by bigville_council_bylaw (cb_beadle_counts/cb_ring_assembly/cb_convene on BELL TIME, block 322000); this seed is retained for its two-tier public/private governance content, and a demonstrator wanting bell-time convening loads bigville_council_bylaw. The now_epoch term-expiry comparisons in the econ seeds are NOT this defect (legitimate in-frame integer timestamps).",
